**Q43 (Loops without Arrays/Strings)**

**Question:** Write a program to check if a number is a strong number.


#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int n, temp, digit, i, fact, sum = 0;

    printf("Enter a number: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    temp = n;

    while (temp > 0)
    {
        digit = temp % 10;
        fact = 1;

        for (i = 1; i <= digit; i++)
        {
            fact = fact * i;
        }

        sum = sum + fact;
        temp = temp / 10;
    }

    if (sum == n)
    {
        printf("%d is a Strong Number", n);
    }
    else
    {
        printf("%d is not a Strong Number", n);
    }

    return 0;
}
```

**Output:**

```text
Enter a number: 145
145 is a Strong Number
```
**Q44 (Loops without Arrays/Strings)**

**Question:** Write a program to find the sum of the series: 1 + 3/4 + 5/6 + 7/8 + … up to n terms.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main()
{
    int n, i;
    float sum = 0;

    printf("Enter the number of terms: ");
    scanf("%d", &n);

    for (i = 1; i <= n; i++)
    {
        sum = sum + (float)(2 * i - 1) / (2 * i);
    }

    printf("Sum of the series = %.2f", sum);

    return 0;
}
```

**Output:**

```text
Enter the number of terms: 4
Sum of the series = 3.14
```
